  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Variant_decodeJsonUnwrapExtensionObject",
    "file": "open62541/src/ua_types_encoding_json.c",
    "description": "On failure while decoding an unwrapped ExtensionObject body, this function calls `UA_free(dst->data)` but leaves `dst->data` pointing to the freed allocation while `dst->type` remains set. The error propagates to `UA_decodeJson`, whose cleanup calls `UA_deleteMembers` on the Variant; `Variant_clear` interprets the dangling pointer as a live typed value and invokes `UA_Array_delete`/`UA_clear`, causing the reported use-after-free in `NodeId_clear`. The same dangling-pointer pattern also exists in the fallback ExtensionObject decode-error branch. Failure cleanup must preserve consistent Variant ownership (typed-clear/delete the partially decoded value as appropriate and set `dst->data = NULL`, or leave it for the outer cleanup), rather than raw-freeing without clearing the pointer.",
    "conditions": "A JSON Variant must declare built-in type 22 (ExtensionObject), contain a Body with a resolvable `TypeId` (the PoV uses numeric Id 785, `CreateSubscriptionRequest`), and then provide malformed or structurally invalid nested Body data so `decodeFields`/the selected structure decoder returns an error after `dst->data` has been allocated. The PoV's malformed nested objects (`{\"Type\":22 \"Body\"{\"Body\"{\"TypeId\"}{}\"TypeId\"}{\"Id\":785}}`) reach this path; the decoder frees the allocated structure, propagates the error, and `UA_decodeJson` error cleanup clears the dangling Variant data a second time."
  },
